content.text:
Uh oh, the mobile board screenshot is very tall and something's wrong: the sticky action dock appears in the middle overlaying suspect cards; suspect grid shows 2 columns with third below, because `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(142px,1fr))` at 390 gives 2 columns. The sticky board-actions is below evidence panel but before suspect panel? Wait markup order: board-grid (evidence panel + suspect panel), then board-actions. In screenshot, after evidence cards, the "select a suspect..." + crime scene + accuse buttons appear, then suspect cards below. That suggests the board-actions is inside? Actually screenshot order: evidence panel, action dock, suspect cards, and no suspect panel heading visible? Let me look: after evidence panel (4 cards), there's the small "SELECT A SUSPECT..." hint, "CRIME SCENE" button, "ACCUSE" button, then suspect cards. This is because board-actions is `position: sticky; bottom: 8px` — in the full-page screenshot, sticky elements render at their stuck position, not the end. Since the full page is tall, it gets stuck at viewport bottom, which in fullPage screenshot composition appears mid-page. That's a screenshot artifact of sticky + fullPage, not actual layout. In actual viewport, the sticky dock stays at bottom while scrolling; it overlaps content but that's intended. However there is an issue: sticky action dock in the middle of the board before suspects. Since the board-grid on mobile is a single column with evidence panel first then suspects, the sticky dock only becomes sticky after its normal position (after the suspect panel). Wait in DOM board-actions comes after board-grid; its normal position is after both panels. Sticky with bottom can stick upward even before reaching its normal position? CSS sticky with bottom works: if element's normal position is below viewport, it shouldn't be displayed early. Yet full-page screenshot artifact places it at a scroll offset. It likely appears at bottom of the initial viewport while the suspect section is below. It's intended. But when at top of board on mobile, the dock should be visible at bottom, sticky (position sticky bottom pins it when its normal position would be below? Actually `position:sticky; bottom:8px` makes it stick when scrolling up? Let's think: sticky with bottom threshold keeps element at least 8px from bottom of scrollport as long as its normal flow position is below the sticky position. At top of page, the element's normal position is farbelow, so it gets pulled up to bottom of viewport. So yes, it shows early. That's okay for UX but it might obscure suspect cards while scrolling—common mobile sticky dock. However it's immediately below evidence in screenshot because full page rendering.

Bigger issue: the board suspect grid uses 2 columns with uneven rows; looks acceptable but third card alone. On 390, each card ~167px; content cramped? It looks tiny text. Better mobile: suspect cards one column, with horizontal layout (mugshot left, content right) for readability. Or 2-column is okay but long vertical. The screenshot shows text at 7-8px unreadable? CSS font sizes are 10.5 dd and 7.5 labels, which at 390 rendered in 2 columns. It's too small. Need improve mobile: single column, larger content, maybe mugshot as banner still. At 390, a single column card width ~330, height ~250; 3 cards -> tall. Could use a horizontal card layout for mobile: mugshot 84x104 on left, details on right, button full width below. This would be compact and more readable. Then desktop 3 columns.

Also "GUN IN HAND" stamp at top right near h1; looks good.

Evidence cards: nice, but bottom "SMOKING GUN" stamp overlaps "Caught in the fabric..." text? It appears red stamp on bottom right overlapping/clipping content? The card has padding-right 18 for p, stamp at bottom right; text may run under. In screenshot, smoking gun stamp is at bottom right, text above. Looks okay, though stamp partially cut? It shows "SMOKING GUN" in red on the card, fine. But note the last evidence card's text ends right at stamp; maybe okay.

The hint/dock button appears before suspects (artifact). On actual mobile, initial board viewport likely shows heading + evidence panel top and sticky dock at bottom, hiding part of the evidence. That's not ideal because dock takes ~120px. But it's useful. Could make it non-sticky on mobile to avoid obscuring evidence; the user can scroll. "works better for mobile" - sticky accusation bar prevents scrolling to find CTA. But dock in mid content artifact suggests sticky could be confusing. I'd prefer a compact sticky dock: just one row with "Accuse" button and selected name, not three stacked rows. Back button could be moved to top or omitted. Then height ~60, less obstruction. On mobile:
- `.board-actions` with hint (maybe hidden) and accuse button only; scene back button moved above as a text link or kept but dock row. Could style dock as horizontal: ghost icon-only back square, hint truncated, accuse button. At 390: 44 + hint 120 + accuse 100 = 264 + gaps, fits. Use `.board-actions` flex-direction row on mobile, hide hint? Let's design: 
  - Dock: back button (square 46 with icon only text hidden), hint (flex), accuse (flex 1.2).
  - But "Accuse" text with arrow. Button width ~140. Hint ~120. Back 46. Total 326 + gaps 18 + padding 22 = 366 fits 390 (minus app 32 => 358 inner; 46+120+140+18+22=346). Tight but doable. Could hide the hint on very small and rely on selection state.
  - Alternative: dock 2 rows: hint row and button row with back icon. Height ~90. Better than 130.
Maybe simplest: on mobile, make dock a single flex row with a back icon-only button and Accuse; hide hint when no selection? Actually hint is valuable. Could put hint above as a normal element outside dock, and dock only contains back + accuse. But hint currently within actions. We can keep hint in dock but font 8, one line, and back icon-only. Height ~60. Good.

Change markup: back button include `<span class="btn-label">Crime scene</span>`; CSS hide label under 900. Then dock row at mobile. `.board-actions{flex-direction:row;align-items:center}` with `.hint{order:0; flex:1; text-align:left; font-size:7.5; line-height:1.35; margin:0}` and buttons. The hint may wrap 2 lines. Height 60-70. Fine. Or hide hint on <380. Good.

But careful: the board action dock appears at bottom of viewport from the start, potentially covering suspect cards. That's expected for a dock. It only covers 60px. Acceptable.

Suspect cards mobile horizontal. Implement:
```
@media(max-width:599px){
 .suspect-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
 .suspect-card{display:grid;grid-template-columns:88px minmax(0,1fr);grid-template-areas:"photo top" "photo dl" "button button";column-gap:11px;padding:11px;align-items:start}
 .mugshot{grid-area:photo;height:100%;min-height:112px;margin:0}
 .suspect-top{grid-area:top}
 .suspect-card dl{grid-area:dl}
 .select-suspect{grid-area:button;margin-top:10px;min-height:42px}
}
```
This will make each card ~200px tall. Text 10.5 still small but better single column. Bump dd to 11.5 and dt 8, role 8. Also heading 17. Good.

Alternatively, allow 2 columns but increase font? The width 160 makes text dense. Single column is better.

Also suspect cards' mugshot on mobile at 88x~130 maybe. Title beside. Good.

Need inspect win/loss.

