content.text:
Now office filing cabinet, cord. Add markup in officeView before office-desk, and after phone maybe cord. CSS.

Markup:
```html
<div class="filing-cabinet" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
...
<div class="desk-cord" aria-hidden="true"></div>
```
Order: window, wall-art, filing-cabinet, office-glow, office-desk, lamp, phone, cord, papers, glass, ashtray, smoke, chips.

CSS:
```
.filing-cabinet{position:absolute;right:4%;bottom:31%;width:11%;height:30%;z-index:2;border:1px solid #534b3c;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#3b3a31,#1d1e18);box-shadow:0 10px 20px #0008}
.filing-cabinet::before{content:'';position:absolute;inset:4% 8% auto;height:3px;background:#615641;opacity:.5}
.filing-cabinet span{position:absolute;left:10%;right:10%;height:25%;border:1px solid #4f493b;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#2e2f27,#181913);box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.04)}
.filing-cabinet span:nth-child(1){top:9%}
... 38,67
.filing-cabinet span::after{content:'';position:absolute;left:41%;top:42%;width:18%;height:5%;border-radius:2px;background:#93805a;opacity:.7}
.desk-cord{position:absolute;right:9%;bottom:26%;width:12%;height:7%;border-bottom:2px solid #141510;border-radius:0 0 50% 50%;transform:rotate(7deg);z-index:5;opacity:.8}
```
The cabinet should be behind the desk; z2 vs desk z4. Great. But placed at bottom 31% height 30 -> from 39% to 69%; desk top 66%. So only bottom 3% covered by desk; cabinet appears tall on wall. Good. Window is at 10-64% left, cabinet right 4-15% width; no overlap. Wall art at right 13-28% top 11-30%; cabinet at right 4-15% top 39-69%; no overlap. Good. But phone at right 16-25% bottom 31-? On desk; cabinet adjacent left (right 4-15%) vs phone right 16-25%. Good.

Add.

